{
  "source": "Prompts/training-bias-2.mp4",
  "duration": 186.7813125,
  "segments": [
    {
      "start": 0.05,
      "end": 2.77,
      "text": "Let's say you ask three people a simple question."
    },
    {
      "start": 3.51,
      "end": 5.05,
      "text": "How much should I study for my exam?"
    },
    {
      "start": 5.99,
      "end": 7.85,
      "text": "Your science teacher says three hours."
    },
    {
      "start": 8.41,
      "end": 12.45,
      "text": "Your mom says 30 minutes because you have to work tonight, and your best friend says"
    },
    {
      "start": 12.45,
      "end": 13.97,
      "text": "studying is overrated."
    },
    {
      "start": 14.73,
      "end": 18.11,
      "text": "Three people you trust give you three completely different answers."
    },
    {
      "start": 18.71,
      "end": 23.15,
      "text": "That happens because each person brings their own specific life experience to the question,"
    },
    {
      "start": 23.59,
      "end": 26.13,
      "text": "and that background naturally shapes the advice they offer."
    },
    {
      "start": 26.75,
      "end": 27.95,
      "text": "You heard three perspectives."
    },
    {
      "start": 28.67,
      "end": 31.13,
      "text": "Imagine an AI learned from only one."
    },
    {
      "start": 31.71,
      "end": 36.15,
      "text": "If a model scraped all of its study advice exclusively from websites written by science teachers,"
    },
    {
      "start": 36.21,
      "end": 38.57,
      "text": "it would internalize that three hours roll."
    },
    {
      "start": 39.09,
      "end": 44.25,
      "text": "When you ask it how much to study, it spits out three hours, as if it is the absolute standard."
    },
    {
      "start": 44.85,
      "end": 45.85,
      "text": "That is training bias."
    },
    {
      "start": 46.61,
      "end": 49.91,
      "text": "The model learned from sources that gave it only a narrow slice of reality."
    },
    {
      "start": 50.75,
      "end": 53.77,
      "text": "Let's look at this board detailing the types of training bias."
    },
    {
      "start": 54.34,
      "end": 57.85,
      "text": "It shows us two distinct ways this problem creeps into AI outputs."
    },
    {
      "start": 58.77,
      "end": 62.77,
      "text": "The first mechanism is when a specific answer shows up too often in the data."
    },
    {
      "start": 63.35,
      "end": 68.11,
      "text": "Because our AI saw three hours repeated constantly across those teacher websites during its training phase,"
    },
    {
      "start": 68.49,
      "end": 71.91,
      "text": "it learned to treat that as its go-to default response for everyone."
    },
    {
      "start": 72.65,
      "end": 75.19,
      "text": "The second mechanism is about what gets left out."
    },
    {
      "start": 75.71,
      "end": 79.23,
      "text": "Students who have to work evening shifts usually aren't the focus of those teacher websites."
    },
    {
      "start": 80.09,
      "end": 82.65,
      "text": "Because they are missing from the training data,"
    },
    {
      "start": 83.29,
      "end": 86.73,
      "text": "the AI has almost no examples of their specific study habits."
    },
    {
      "start": 87.39,
      "end": 89.81,
      "text": "If a perspective is absent from the training examples,"
    },
    {
      "start": 90.39,
      "end": 92.63,
      "text": "the AI's final advice will overlook it."
    },
    {
      "start": 93.31,
      "end": 96.07,
      "text": "You can spot this happening in everyday interactions."
    },
    {
      "start": 96.69,
      "end": 99.71,
      "text": "Say you ask an AI to generate a list of successful entrepreneurs."
    },
    {
      "start": 100.67,
      "end": 101.91,
      "text": "It prints out 10 names."
    },
    {
      "start": 102.59,
      "end": 105.59,
      "text": "But as you read through them, you notice they are all tech founders."
    },
    {
      "start": 106.23,
      "end": 107.57,
      "text": "You look at that list and think,"
    },
    {
      "start": 107.57,
      "end": 110.19,
      "text": "wait, why are all 10 in tech?"
    },
    {
      "start": 111.23,
      "end": 116.79,
      "text": "So you type a follow-up, asking who else would make the list if we looked outside the technology sector."
    },
    {
      "start": 117.69,
      "end": 119.51,
      "text": "The list tells you which industry showed up."
    },
    {
      "start": 119.95,
      "end": 121.87,
      "text": "You need more evidence to know why."
    },
    {
      "start": 122.79,
      "end": 127.35,
      "text": "Before we look at the toolkit, what specific instruction would you type to the AI right now"
    },
    {
      "start": 127.35,
      "end": 129.37,
      "text": "to force it to change its pattern?"
    },
    {
      "start": 130.39,
      "end": 132.37,
      "text": "Recognizing the bias is only the first step."
    },
    {
      "start": 132.37,
      "end": 137.91,
      "text": "You need precise phrasing to force the model to look past its most heavily weighted data clusters."
    },
    {
      "start": 138.91,
      "end": 141.55,
      "text": "This graphic provides a three-step toolkit for those moments"
    },
    {
      "start": 141.55,
      "end": 144.15,
      "text": "when you suspect an answer is shaped by training bias."
    },
    {
      "start": 144.89,
      "end": 147.69,
      "text": "First, try asking, what's missing from this answer?"
    },
    {
      "start": 148.49,
      "end": 153.19,
      "text": "Second, instruct the model, show me examples that don't fit the pattern you just gave."
    },
    {
      "start": 153.99,
      "end": 157.79,
      "text": "And third, tell it, answer again, leaving out the most famous examples."
    },
    {
      "start": 158.49,
      "end": 161.47,
      "text": "These prompts are highly effective for interrogating the model,"
    },
    {
      "start": 161.47,
      "end": 162.63,
      "text": "but they aren't magic."
    },
    {
      "start": 163.43,
      "end": 167.81,
      "text": "If the missing perspective simply wasn't included in the underlying training data,"
    },
    {
      "start": 168.45,
      "end": 170.69,
      "text": "the AI cannot pull it out of thin air."
    },
    {
      "start": 171.37,
      "end": 177.09,
      "text": "Let's review this summary graphic, which contains the foundational rule for working with generative tools."
    },
    {
      "start": 177.81,
      "end": 180.17,
      "text": "AI learns from its training data."
    },
    {
      "start": 180.75,
      "end": 183.23,
      "text": "Bias in the data can shape the answer."
    }
  ],
